  "question": {
    "text": "A circular disk of radius R meter and mass M kg is rotating around the axis perpendicular to the disk. An external torque is applied to the disk such that $\\theta(t)=5 t^2-8 t$, where $\\theta(t)$ is the angular position of the rotating disc as a function of time $t$.\nHow much power is delivered by the applied torque, when $t=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$72 \\mathrm{MR}^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$8 \\mathrm{MR}^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$108 \\mathrm{MR}^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$60 \\mathrm{MR}^2$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\theta=5 \\mathrm{t}^2-8 \\mathrm{t} \\\\\n& \\omega=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\theta}{\\mathrm{dt}}=10 \\mathrm{t}-8 \\\\\n& \\alpha=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\omega}{\\mathrm{dt}}=10 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{p}=\\tau \\omega \\\\\n& =(\\mathrm{I} \\alpha) \\omega \\\\\n& =\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{mR}^2}{2}\\right) \\alpha \\omega \\\\\n& =\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{mR}^2}{2}\\right)(10)(10\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nPut $\\mathrm{t}=2$\n$\\mathrm{p}=60 \\mathrm{mR}^2$"
  }
}